            <ArticleTitle>Periodontal and alveolar bone abnormalities associated with pachydermoperiostosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pachydermoperiostosis (PDP) is an unusual syndrome manifested clinically by finger clubbing, extremity enlargement, hypertrophic skin changes, and periosteal bone formation. A rare case of pachydermoperiostosis (primary hypertrophic osteoarthropathy) with oral manifestations in a 47-year-old man is presented. The possible correlation between physiological mechanisms of this disease and their influence on oral periodontal tissues and alveolar bone is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
